---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /s.html
title: "Share channels"
description: "Channels for Ferrite radios as a QR code or a link: scan it with Ferrite Pocket to add them to your radio."
---
<div class="wrap column share">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1 id="share-title">Share channels</h1>
    <p class="lead" id="share-lead">Channels for Ferrite radios as a QR code or a link. Scan it with <b>Ferrite
      Pocket</b> on a phone and the channels are added to your radio, at free channel numbers, so nothing you have
      changes.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section" id="view" hidden>
    <p class="kicker" id="view-what"></p>
    <div class="tablewrap"><table id="view-table"></table></div>
    <p><a class="btn solid" id="view-open" href="ferrite://share">Open in Ferrite Pocket</a></p>
    <p class="muted" id="view-note"></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="make">
    <p class="kicker"><span>01</span>Make a code</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>For a club net, a hamfest or a conference: type the frequencies, then put the QR code on your website,
        a slide or a badge. Two or more channels go as a zone, named below.</p>
    </div>
    <form id="make-form" class="share-form" autocomplete="off">
      <label class="share-zone">Zone name <small>(for two or more channels; 16 characters)</small>
        <input name="zone" maxlength="16" placeholder="DEF CON 34">
      </label>
      <div id="make-rows"></div>
      <p><button type="button" class="btn" id="make-add">Add a channel</button></p>
    </form>
    <p class="muted" id="make-error"></p>

    <div id="make-out" class="share-out" hidden>
      <div class="share-qr" id="make-qr"></div>
      <div class="share-links">
        <p class="kicker"><span>02</span>Use it</p>
        <p><input id="make-link" readonly class="share-link"></p>
        <p>
          <button type="button" class="btn solid" id="make-copy">Copy the link</button>
          <a class="btn" id="make-svg" download="ferrite-channels.svg">Download SVG</a>
          <a class="btn" id="make-png" download="ferrite-channels.png">Download PNG</a>
        </p>
        <p class="muted" id="make-size"></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <noscript><p>Making a code needs JavaScript; it all happens in your browser.</p></noscript>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h3>What's in a code</h3>
    <p>Only the channels: names, frequencies, mode, tones, shift and power, any site positions, and the zone's name.
      No callsign and nothing else from a radio. The code is the part of the link after the <code>#</code>, which a
      browser never sends to a website: this page reads and makes codes in your browser, and nothing is stored.</p>
    <p>Each channel goes at the first free number on the radio that adds it; tones and power can be changed there
      afterwards. The radio refuses anything outside its bands or its region's transmit rules, as it does any
      channel.</p>
  </section>
</div>

<script src="/assets/qrcode.js"></script>
<script type="module" src="/assets/share.js"></script>
